From c6238fc3deb50cefae5aaa1efba6daa8645ed238 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jordanrb188 <jordaneeuu18@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 03:14:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: harden socket authorization and business-hour
 pricing

Calculate night and peak surcharges in America/Caracas through Intl,
configurable with BUSINESS_TIME_ZONE, instead of reading the server
clock. Fares and multipliers are unchanged.

Verify trip ownership from the signed session before cancelling a ride,
reject cancellations of trips that are already closed, and report every
refusal through rideCancellationRejected.

Scope every broadcast: administrative events reach the admins room only,
locations reach administration and the participants of the active trip,
and driver profiles are no longer emitted to the whole fleet. The former
global emits leaked the bcrypt password hash of every connecting driver.

Validate driver status and coordinates from one module shared by REST and
Socket.IO, always resolving the driver from socket.data.auth so a payload
identifier can no longer modify another driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
