From 53bf3de1a30d09fb5156480060f51b83c7049ca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jordanrb188 <jordaneeuu18@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 03:48:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: harden ride acceptance and canonicalise trip
 broadcasts

Require an active dispatch session whose current driver matches the
signed session before accepting a ride, and verify the trip exists and
is still SEARCHING before touching the lock, timers or session. The
transition is guarded and the lock reverted on failure, so a hostile
event can no longer assign a ride that was never offered.

Wrap socket handlers so a non-object payload is normalised and any
throw stays contained. A literal null bypassed the `= {}` default, so
destructuring threw synchronously and killed the whole process: any
authenticated client could stop the server with one malformed event.

Stop creating trips from an inbound rideRequested event. POST
/api/trips/create is now the only path, and passengers emitting the
event get rideRequestFailed with USE_REST_API. The outbound offer to
the selected driver keeps the same name and behaviour.

Build tripStatusUpdated payloads on the server from the persisted trip
instead of rebroadcasting the driver's object, so injected fields never
reach passengers or administration, and send the driver only as a
summary without email, cedula, documents or wallet balance.

The dispatch integration test now creates its trip over REST, since the
socket path it previously used no longer creates trips. Every assertion
in that test is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
